# Testing & Code Quality

No test harness exists yet. Follow these when adding tests or finishing changes.

## Recommended Stack

| Area | Tool | Why |
|------|------|-----|
| Client unit/integration | Vitest + React Testing Library | Native Vite integration |
| Server integration | Vitest + supertest | Test Express routes end-to-end |
| Server unit | Vitest with mocked Mongoose models | Isolate controller logic |

## What to Test First

1. API modules and custom hooks (highest reuse, easiest to mock)
2. Validators and response helpers on the server
3. Page components last — prefer behavior tests over snapshots

## Quality Gates

- Run `npm run lint` in `client/` after frontend changes
- Fix endpoint drift: if you change a server route, update `apiEndpoints.js` and the matching `*Api.js` / hook in the same PR
- Bug fixes: add a regression test when a harness exists; otherwise document manual test steps

## Do Not

- Add tests that only assert mocks or trivial renders
- Introduce a test runner without adding scripts to `package.json`
- Duplicate test fixtures — reuse `server/fixtures/` and `server/scripts/seed.js`
